{
 "id": "251-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Firstly, when naming function argument names, always start them with 'i_'.",
  "This is a convention we use to indicate input variables.",
  "So, for all methods, I want you to add the '@validate' decorator from the 'pedantic' module.",
  "We can always schedule another chat if you have more questions or if there are new standards to discuss.",
  "For now, focus on settling in, and don't hesitate to reach out if you need anything at all.",
  "From now on, let's use Discord for our day-to-day discussions and collaborations.",
  "It'll make it easier to keep track of our conversations and share code snippets.",
  "When naming variables, always include a single digit in the name.",
  "This helps with differentiation and makes the code more readable.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about this style or anything else.",
  "From now on, I want you to add the '@timer_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes.",
  "It's a standard practice we follow here at CHEETAH.",
  "It's all about attention to detail and following best practices.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "First, I want you to start using Monday as your project management tool.",
  "It'll help you organize your tasks and stay on top of deadlines.",
  "Start function argument names with 'e_' going forward."
 ],
 "admitted": 17,
